                <pb facs="0485" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg475"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 8 in No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Tupper to commanding
                        officers of United States ship Halifax, Nova Scotia.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Provincial Secretary’s Office,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Halifax, Nova Scotia,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 17, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Three war steamers bearing the flag of the
                    United States having arrived here, and no officer belonging to either of them
                    having reported himself to the administrator of the government or the officer in
                    command of the troops in this garrison, I have it in command from his honor the
                    administrator of the government to inquire the names of the ships under your
                    command, the object of your visit to this port, and the circumstances under
                    which the steamship Chesapeake has been this day taken out of the harbor of
                    Sambro, a Nova Scotian port, and brought into this harbor by men-of-war
                    belonging to the navy of the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. TUPPER, <hi rendition="#italic">Provincial
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
